# winemac-crossprocess-remote-layer.patch — the wine half of the cross-process Steam fix.
# APPLYABLE DIFF, regenerated from the working tree on 2026-09-02. The earlier prose version of
# this file (six dated addenda) is preserved at docs/winemac-crossprocess-remote-layer-history.md.
#
# WARNING: AI-AUTHORED. Read this before you read the code.
#
# This patch was written with heavy AI assistance. 3Shain/dxmt's CONTRIBUTING.md cannot accept
# AI-authored contributions, so it was never offered as a PR; the findings went upstream as reports
# instead: https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt/issues/141#issuecomment-5477055980 and
# https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60263. It is published here on purpose, MIT-licensed like
# the rest of this repo; you are welcome to use, adapt or rewrite it under those terms. If you are
# a wine or dxmt maintainer who intends to write your own implementation, reading this file is a
# choice with a consequence: the reports carry the whole diagnosis with none of the code.
#
# WHAT IT DOES (dlls/winemac.drv; five files):
#   - implements the FIXME "Cross-process child window Metal swapchains are not implemented":
#     a foreign CHILD hwnd gets its CAContext swapchain built against its ROOT, which owns the
#     NSWindow and lives in the owning process; the child hwnd rides in wParam so the owner can
#     position the hosted CALayerHost at the child's rect in the root's space (Win32 pixels
#     converted to Cocoa points at the Cocoa entry points)
#   - stacks hosted layers by Win32 paint order (zPosition), not creation order
#   - hides a 0x0 child instead of stretching it over the view; treats CGRectNull as "no rect"
#   - retires a superseded layer on CREATE, not destroy, so a child is never unhosted mid-resize
#   - exports dxmt_acquire_remote_layer / dxmt_release_remote_layer as standalone symbols (dlsym
#     from DXMT; NOT a macdrv_functions_t member, which would be an ABI break); surfaces keyed by
#     view, one retired surface held per child hwnd, dead children drained and pruned
#   - keeps a compiled-out resize diagnostic (-DDXMT_RSZ_DEBUG)
#
# APPLY: to a wine 11.16 tree that already carries scripts/wineandaqua-dxmt.patch (aquadran's DXMT
# support), from the tree root:  patch -p1 < winemac-crossprocess-remote-layer.patch
# Requires wine >= 11.11 (the CAContext/CALayerHost route this builds on landed there).
# Rebuild just the module:  gmake dlls/winemac.drv/winemac.so
# Pairs with scripts/dxmt-remote-layer-fallback.patch; NEITHER half works alone.
#
# VERIFIED 2026-09-02 on the installed module (sha256 310f13d0...): Steam renders out-of-process
# with text, 0 GPU crashes over three sessions; library/friends/settings/store/downloads all
# render; 2400x1500 -> 2399x1499 -> 2400x1500 measures interior luminance 83/84/112 with 0 bright
# edges; two 40-sample churns + a static control at 0 gap frames; the game boots to MainMenu.
#
